  "notes": "12-segment, 11-point lathe (216 triangles), one closed shell, no boolean and no self-intersection.  Body whorl is the widest ring at 60 mm; the top is cut into two terraces that step up to a 46 mm apex.  A shear above the body whorl (0.55 x height) makes the spire lean 12 mm off centre so the terraces read as a coil.  Suture = one angular bulge per ring advancing 1.6 turns bottom to top (amplitude 7.5%).  Mouth = at rings 2-4 the 0-degree column is pulled 34% in while its +-1 column neighbours are pushed 26% out, giving a recessed mouth inside a raised lip.  Materials by face centre before the shear: the mouth pocket (+15 degrees, z 10-30 mm) and the suture line (|delta| < 0.32 rad) are wood_dark, the band beside the suture (0.36-1.00 rad) is wool, the rest shell.  fit_bounds pins 60 x 55 x 50 mm.",
